cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use anchor in your research, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "anchor: endpoint-anchored dead-reckoned trajectory reconstruction and behaviour inference for elasmobranch biologger data"
abstract: >-
  anchor reconstructs fine-scale animal trajectories from archival
  accelerometer/IMU tags via a constrained sequential Monte Carlo particle
  filter (tide, bathymetry, wind-leeway and Verified-Position constraints with
  FFBS smoothing), classifies behaviour from kinematics (HMM and supervised,
  with subject-level cross-validation), and turns the K joint trajectory samples
  into uncertainty-propagated utilization distributions and energy seascapes.
type: software
